<article class="env-exercise" id="02DU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02DU">Exercise <span data-tag="02DU">111.22.6</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Suppose that $M$ is a finite locally free $A$-module, and suppose that $\varphi : M \to M$ is an endomorphism. Define/construct the <em>trace</em> and <em>determinant</em> of $\varphi $ and prove that your construction is “functorial in the triple $(A, M, \varphi )$”. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Show that if $M, N$ are finite locally free $A$-modules, and if $\varphi : M \to N$ and $\psi : N \to M$ then $\text{Trace}(\varphi \circ \psi ) = \text{Trace}(\psi \circ \varphi )$ and $\det (\varphi \circ \psi ) = \det (\psi \circ \varphi )$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
In case $M$ is finite locally free show that $\text{Trace}$ defines an $A$-linear map $\text{End}_ A(M) \to A$ and $\det $ defines a multiplicative map $\text{End}_ A(M) \to A$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>